================================================================================
Demo catalog data
================================================================================

Synthetic demo catalog generated by backend/scripts/generate_catalog.py (MIT). Every brand and product in it is invented.

The demo storefront ("Nimbus") ships a committed, signed product catalog bundle at
`backend/examples/catalog/` (720 products, 12 categories, 60 each). It is built from
`backend/examples/source/catalog.csv`, which is the output of
`backend/scripts/generate_catalog.py` run over the committed vocabulary in
`backend/src/edgereco/catalog/synthetic_vocab.json`. The brands, product names,
feature text, prices and ratings are all made up for this repository. The product
images are generated SVG cards (`edgereco.catalog.product_image`). No third-party
dataset, scraped content or photo is included, so no third-party attribution is
required. The catalog is covered by this repository's MIT license.

Category names (for example "Home & Kitchen") are ordinary descriptive shelf names.
Technology names such as Bluetooth and USB-C are used only to describe what kind of
connector or wireless standard an invented product has.

Regenerate it with:

    cd backend
    uv run python scripts/generate_catalog.py
    uv run python scripts/gen_demo_sessions.py
    uv run python scripts/rebuild_example_bundle.py --from-source

Earlier versions of this repository (before the synthetic catalog) shipped a subset
of a third-party Amazon product dataset. That data is no longer in the current tree.
